        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(active-memory): normalize legacy toggle timestamps",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Active Memory doctor migration accepted any numeric legacy `updatedAt` value. JSON overflow values can parse to `Infinity`, which would be imported into plugin state instead of being normalized.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe migration now accepts only finite legacy timestamps and falls back to `Date.now()` for malformed values, matching the existing fallback behavior for non-number timestamps.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDoctor migration no longer writes non-finite timestamps into Active Memory session-toggle state. Valid finite timestamps are preserved.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_FS_MODULE_CACHE_PATH=/tmp/openclaw-vitest-cache-active-memory-doctor-reviewfix node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/active-memory/doctor-contract-api.test.ts`\n- `oxfmt --check` and `oxlint` on `extensions/active-memory/doctor-contract-api.ts` and `extensions/active-memory/doctor-contract-api.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Claude autoreview: clean after review fix and rebase to `upstream/main`\n\n## Proof\n\nThe regression test writes a raw legacy JSON file with `updatedAt: 1e999`, verifies the migration imports the toggle, and proves the imported timestamp is the fixed `Date.now()` value rather than a non-finite number.\n",
